          "text": "Abdominal and renal angle examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Abdomen soft and non-tender, no mass or suprapubic distension; no costovertebral angle tenderness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Urinary voiding history"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Voids 5–6 times daily and once overnight. Stream is slow but unchanged and described as the same as always. Reports often holding urine at work. Reports drinking lots of coffee and energy drinks and probably not enough water."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Reported associated symptoms and pertinent negatives"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "For the rash, no vesicles, weeping, or pain. No shortness of breath, wheeze, lip or tongue swelling, fever, systemic symptoms, or recent viral illness. No genital rash, dysuria, or discharge. For urinary history, no current haematuria, loin pain, or suprapubic pain; no UTI in more than 1 year."
      }
    },
